  "title": "Journal becomes a validated, indexed run store",
  "summary": "The journal grows from a single hash-chained buffer file into a small subsystem: a versioned event model with ten payload types, a JSON Schema every event is validated against before it is written, a canonical hash layout plus a separate replay digest, a per-work-item run index guarded by a file lock, and a reader that refuses a broken chain rather than returning a partial one. The buffer directory becomes `runs/`, `osf run start`/`osf run complete` are new CLI entry points, and the checkpoint and review runners now write typed actors and evidence grades.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
